{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Lemmas","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorSpectralCubicGeometry","lean:module:QOU.Mass.DilationBranchLocusRigidity"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.qsquare_shift_not_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.qsquare_shift_not_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L284-L289","doc":"The same statement for the shift the W1 route actually asks for, `l = q²` with\n`q > 1`: the substrate shift is not of order `2`, at any nonzero point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.dilation_gt_one_not_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.dilation_gt_one_not_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L268-L282","doc":"**A dilation by a factor `> 1` is not an involution.** Combined with\n`DilationBranchLocusRigidity.dilation_scaling_rigid` and `inversion_rigid` above, the\nmonomial maps preserving the branch locus are exactly `id` and `ι`, both of order at most\n`2`; a substrate shift `z ↦ l·z` with `l = q₀² > 1` squares to `z ↦ l²·z`, which moves\nevery nonzero point. So no monomial base automorphism supplies the W1 q-shift.\n\nStated for any real `l > 1` so that no numerical value enters the Lean, exactly as in\n`DilationBranchLocusRigidity.no_scaling_of_one_lt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.no_inversion_of_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.no_inversion_of_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L259-L262","doc":"**No inversion other than `ι` preserves the branch locus.** Contrapositive form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.inversion_rigid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.inversion_rigid","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L238-L257","doc":"**Inversion rigidity of the branch locus.** If `z ↦ l/z` sends the branch sextic to a\nconstant multiple of itself, then `l = 1` and the constant is `1` — i.e. the only\ninversion preserving the branch locus is the palindromic `ι : z ↦ 1/z` itself.\n\nThe `z⁶` coefficient gives `16 = c·16`, hence `c = 1`; the `z⁵` coefficient then gives\n`24·l = 24`, hence `l = 1`. Characteristic zero is used only to invert those two\nintegers — the same two that carry `DilationBranchLocusRigidity.dilation_scaling_rigid`,\none coefficient-index apart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.eval_invSexticPoly_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.eval_invSexticPoly_eq","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L227-L234","doc":"`invSexticPoly l` really does evaluate to `z⁶ · D(l/z)`, so the hypothesis of\n`inversion_rigid` below is the honest \"`z ↦ l/z` sends `D` to a multiple of itself\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.invSexticPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.invSexticPoly","kind":"def","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L212-L217","doc":"The polynomial `z ↦ z⁶ · D(l/z)`, coefficients read off. `D` has degree `6`, so\nclearing the denominator gives a polynomial again — with the coefficient list reversed\nand `l`-weighted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.base_involution_ne_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.base_involution_ne_id","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L189-L200","doc":"The base involution is **not** the identity: `ι` genuinely has order `2`.\n\nCharacteristic zero is not decoration here — the statement is **false** in characteristic\n`2`, where `𝔽₂`'s only unit is `1` and `1⁻¹ = 1`, so `ι` *is* the identity on `𝔽₂ˣ`. The\nwitness `z = 2` works exactly because `2⁻¹ = 2` would force `1 = 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.invLift_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.invLift_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L183-L187","doc":"**`ι̃` is an involution.** Applying `(X, z) ↦ (X/z, 1/z)` twice returns `(X, z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.mem_sigma_of_mem_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.mem_sigma_of_mem_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L174-L181","doc":"**`ι̃` maps `Σ` to `Σ`.** If `(X, z)` is a point of the curve with `z ≠ 0`, so is\n`(X/z, 1/z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.colorCubic_inv_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.colorCubic_inv_lift","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L164-L172","doc":"**The lift identity.** `z³ · P(X/z, 1/z) = P(X, z)` for every `z ≠ 0`.\n\nThis is the palindromy of the *cubic's* coefficient list — `a_k(1/z) = z^{k−3} a_k(z)` —\nrather than of the branch sextic, and it is what makes the base involution lift. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.branchSextic_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.branchSextic_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L151-L154","doc":"`D(-1) = 4 ≠ 0` in characteristic zero: the fibre over `z = -1` is unramified too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.branchSextic_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.branchSextic_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L146-L149","doc":"Both fixed fibres are **unramified**: `D(1) = 200 ≠ 0` in characteristic zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.fibre_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.fibre_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L141-L144","doc":"The fibre over `z = 1` is `X³ + 2X² + 3X + 4`. `ι̃` acts there by `X ↦ X/1 = X`, so\nall three of its points are fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.origin_mem_sigma_at_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.origin_mem_sigma_at_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L137-L139","doc":"`(0, -1)` really is a point of `Σ`: the fixed point over `z = -1` exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.fibre_at_neg_one_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.fibre_at_neg_one_factors","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L132-L135","doc":"The fibre over `z = -1`: `P(X, -1) = X(X²+1)`. Since `ι̃` acts there by `X ↦ -X`,\nits unique fixed point over `z = -1` is `X = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.fibre_at_zero_factors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.fibre_at_zero_factors","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L128-L130","doc":"The fibre over `z = 0`: `P(X, 0) = (X+1)(X²+1)`, three distinct sheets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.colorCubic_coeff_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.colorCubic_coeff_form","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L122-L126","doc":"The coefficient closed form, made explicit: `a_k = ∑_{i≤3−k} z^i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.colorCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.PalindromicInvolutionLift.colorCubic","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/PalindromicInvolutionLift.lean#L116-L120","doc":"The **colour spectral cubic** `P(X, z) = X³ + (z+1)X² + (z²+z+1)X + (z³+z²+z+1)`,\nwhose vanishing locus is `Σ`. Its coefficients are the truncated geometric sums\n`a_k = 1 + z + ⋯ + z^(3−k)`, which is exactly why the palindromic involution lifts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}